    "setting": {
        "title": "Pathfinder",
        "url_slug": "pathfinder-1",
        "description": "[B]Pathfinder First Edition (1e)[/B] is a tabletop role-playing game published by Paizo in 2009. Designed as a refined evolution of Dungeons & Dragons 3.5 under the Open Game License (OGL), it is frequently referred to as \"D&D 3.75.\"\n\n[LIST]\n[*][B]Core Mechanics:[/B] Built on the traditional [B]d20 system[/B] (rolling a 20-sided die + modifiers against a target difficulty class).\n[*][B]Character Customization:[/B] Offers immense build depth with dozens of classes, archetypes, feats, and spells, catering heavily to system mastery and theorycrafting (often nicknamed \"Mathfinder\").\n[*][B]Setting:[/B] Set in the rich high-fantasy world of [B]Golarion[/B], which blends classic fantasy with elements of cosmic horror, steampunk, planar travel, and sword-and-sorcery.\n[*][B]Adventure Paths:[/B] Famous for its epic, multi-volume pre-written campaigns from level 1 to 20 (e.g., [I]Rise of the Runelords[/I], [I]Kingmaker[/I], [I]Wrath of the Righteous[/I]).\n[*][B]Tactical Depth:[/B] Features crunchy, grid-based combat with comprehensive rules for combat maneuvers, positioning, and attacks of opportunity.\n[/LIST]",
        "heading": "",
        "archetype_heading": "Rasse & Klasse",
        "image_url": "images/pathfinder-logo2.png",
